Preserve generated DOS aliases when deleting a cached regular file.

CacheOut rebuilt every remaining alias after each unlink. A wildcard search
kept its original aliases and consequently skipped or addressed other files.
Remove only the deleted cache entry; retain both other aliases and independent
FindFirst/FindNext snapshots. Directory removal keeps its existing invalidation.

